The ascension in itself wasn't very interesting, but I'll give a few 
details to prepare the story.  There were VERY VERY few potions of any 
kind of healing at all and only one nurse, but I ended up with fifteen 
amulets of life saving (and six of almost every important kind of ring, 
though that doesn't matter here).  Also, I found a few too many bones 
piles with too much of the ascension kit, so I decided to make it at 
least infinitesimally harder by not wishing...despite having two wands of 
wishing (found the second one in Ghennom) and six magic lamps. 
So, I felt pretty prepared when I got to the planes.  Earth was very 
easy...but then came fire.  That should  have been easy too, but it 
started with an Archon who summoned immediately.  And in the first 
summoning came another one.  They just kept summoning and at one point I 
counted TEN archons a summoning.  The portal was only about ten to 
fifteen squares away, but somehow that felt pretty damn far.  This was a 
wizard who was wielding magicbane, so I kept dropping the amulet to cast.  
However, I also like to levitate on fire so that fumblefingers doesn't 
send her characters into the lava...again.
So, about when I had five archons summoning I figured it was safe to put 
down the amulet for a bit...not like I was about to need it and I reallly 
needed the charming.  Let it suffice to say that it took every single 
potion of full healing I had (and I'd brought twelve...which I thought 
should have been enough) and still there were about eight squares to the 
portal and more archons than ever.
Then a captain with a wand of death killed the cockatrice I'd been 
headingi towards....and an archon picked up the corpse when it was Right 
next to me (if it had been further, conflict would have been nice.)  
As it was, I was just glad that I still had ten amulets of life saving 
and two lizard corpses left.  I got to eat the lizard in bites, because 
after every bite I was interupted...by an archon who hit me with a rubber 
chicken.  I had chances to hit the archon, but the problem was that there 
were Two archons right next to me and they were fast enough that I rarely 
got a chance to hit them...certainly not enough of a chance to kill both.
To  make a long story short, I ate both lizards and used every single 
amulet...on my last life I managed to kill the right Archon and the 
cockatrice corpse made it easy enough to get to the portal.  Even Astral 
was a piece of cake after that.

